===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|pilier}} , from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{m|la|pilare||a pillar}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|pila||a pillar, pier, mole}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/ˈpɪlɚ/|lang=en}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈpɪlə/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-pillar.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɪlə(ɹ)|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|pil|lar|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{label|en|architecture}} A large [[post]], often used as supporting architecture.
# Something resembling such a structure.
#: ''a '''pillar''' of smoke''
# An essential part of something that provides support.
#: ''He's a '''pillar''' of the community.''
# {{label|en|Roman Catholic}} A portable ornamental column, formerly carried before a cardinal, as emblematic of his support to the church.
#: {{rfquotek|Skelton}}
# The centre of the [[volta]], [[ring]], or [[manege]] ground, around which a [[horse]] turns.

